      "hardware_label": "Intel Arc Pro B70",
      "notes": "Qwen3.6 27B AutoRound INT4 one-B70 vLLM/XPU strict fresh-response result with default-off runtime INT8 lm_head projection enabled (VLLM_XPU_LM_HEAD_INT8=1). This is labeled separately from the original BF16-LM-head AutoRound quantization: the BF16 lm_head remains resident, but the projection uses a transient per-output-channel INT8 weight copy plus per-token INT8 activation quantization. Primary metric is median generated-token throughput for tokens 1-100 after TTFT across the fixed realistic prompt suite. Each prompt was sent once; cached_tokens=0 for every request; no prompt/KV cache reuse, context checkpoints, response reuse, n-gram/history acceleration, or warmed repeated prompts. qwen3_next_mtp accepted tokens are verified by the target model. Full quality gate passed and matched baseline, including 32-repeat stability and the 1K long-context needle. Same-window BF16-lm-head control was 53.33 tok/s; INT8 repeat was 62.28 tok/s.",
